      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds like you are dealing with a deep, existential form of guilt that goes far beyond just having made an error. When the impact feels existential, the usual advice falls short because the pain is tied to your sense of self. Instead of trying to \"move past\" it immediately, perhaps focus on understanding the gravity of the situation by seeking professional guidance to navigate responsibility. A therapist can help you differentiate between the terrible *action* you took and the core *worth* of the person you are.",
      "source": "target",
